IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`

-- PART 3 -- REQUIRED PERIOD CONDITION: regulations 12 to 15B.
--
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Regs 12 and 13 say what C must be likely to be found, at every time in two
-- windows, for the standard and the enhanced rate of each component. Regs 14 to 15B fix the "prescribed
-- date" the two windows hang from, and in three after-an-interval cases shift the windows.
--
-- What is "likely" is the Secretary of State's prediction of the Secretary of State's own determination
-- (fork F-2): the facts about it are inputs, phrased as the conditional.

§ `Regulations 12 and 13: the required period condition`

-- The facts regs 12 and 13 ask about, for one component: at every time in each window, which level of
-- ability the Secretary of State would likely determine. "Limited" here means limited ability and not
-- severely limited ability (reg 4(3): severely limited is not also limited).
DECLARE `the likely determinations across the two windows` HAS
    `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months ending with the prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months ending with the prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "Limited" in regs 12(1) and 13(1) is limited ability and not severely limited ability (reg 4(3): severely limited is
-- not also limited), at every time in the window.
GIVEN d IS A `the likely determinations across the two windows`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regs 12 and 13: only limited ability is likely at every time in the 3 months ending with the prescribed date` d MEANS
        d's `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months ending with the prescribed date`
    AND (NOT d's `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months ending with the prescribed date`)

GIVEN d IS A `the likely determinations across the two windows`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regs 12 and 13: only limited ability is likely at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date` d MEANS
        d's `limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date`
    AND (NOT d's `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date`)

-- Limb (a) of regs 12(1) and 13(1): met where only limited ability is likely at every time in the 3 months ending with
-- the prescribed date, or where reg 15A(4) or 15B(4) regards it as met.
GIVEN d IS A `the likely determinations across the two windows`
      `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regs 12(1)(a) and 13(1)(a): limb (a) is met` d `with` `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` MEANS
       `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)`
    OR `regs 12 and 13: only limited ability is likely at every time in the 3 months ending with the prescribed date` d

-- Limb (a) of regs 12(2) and 13(2): the same with severely limited ability.
GIVEN d IS A `the likely determinations across the two windows`
      `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regs 12(2)(a) and 13(2)(a): limb (a) is met` d `with` `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` MEANS
       `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)`
    OR d's `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 3 months ending with the prescribed date`

-- reg 12(1): C meets the required period condition for the purposes of section 78(1) of the Act (daily
-- living component at standard rate) where (a) if C had been assessed at every time in the 3 months ending
-- with the prescribed date, it is likely that the Secretary of State would have determined at that time that
-- C had limited ability to carry out daily living activities; and (b) if C were to be assessed at every time
-- in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date, it is likely that the Secretary of State
-- would determine at that time that C had limited ability.
-- The look-back limb (a) is regarded as met where reg 15A(4) or 15B(4) says so (the input).
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 s 78(1)
-- src:105 | (1) C meets the required period condition for the purposes of section 78(1) of the Act (daily living component at standard rate) where —
-- src:106 | (a) if C had been assessed at every time in the period of 3 months ending with the prescribed date, it is likely that the Secretary of State would have determined at that time that C had limited ability to carry out daily living activities; and
-- src:107 | (b) if C were to be assessed at every time in the period of 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date, it is likely that the Secretary of State would determine at that time that C had limited ability to carry out daily living activities.
@ref reg 12(1) (src:105-107)
GIVEN d IS A `the likely determinations across the two windows`
      `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 12(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the daily living component is met` d `with` `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` MEANS
        `regs 12(1)(a) and 13(1)(a): limb (a) is met` d `with` `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)`
    AND `regs 12 and 13: only limited ability is likely at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date` d

-- reg 12(2): the same for section 78(2) of the Act (daily living component at enhanced rate), severely limited ability.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 s 78(2)
-- src:108 | (2) C meets the required period condition for the purposes of section 78(2) of the Act (daily living component at enhanced rate) where —
-- src:109 | (a) if C had been assessed at every time in the period of 3 months ending with the prescribed date, it is likely that the Secretary of State would have determined at that time that C had severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities; and
-- src:110 | (b) if C were to be assessed at every time in the period of 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date, it is likely that the Secretary of State would determine at that time that C had severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities.
@ref reg 12(2) (src:108-110)
GIVEN d IS A `the likely determinations across the two windows`
      `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 12(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the daily living component is met` d `with` `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` MEANS
        `regs 12(2)(a) and 13(2)(a): limb (a) is met` d `with` `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)`
    AND d's `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date`

-- reg 13(1) and (2): the same for the mobility component (sections 79(1) and 79(2) of the Act).
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 s 79(1), s 79(2)
-- src:112 | (1) C meets the required period condition for the purposes of section 79(1) of the Act (mobility component at standard rate) where —
-- src:113 | (a) if C had been assessed at every time in the period of 3 months ending with the prescribed date, it is likely that the Secretary of State would have determined at that time that C had limited ability to carry out mobility activities; and
-- src:114 | (b) if C were to be assessed at every time in the period of 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date, it is likely that the Secretary of State would determine at that time that C had limited ability to carry out mobility activities.
@ref reg 13(1) (src:112-114)
GIVEN d IS A `the likely determinations across the two windows`
      `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 13(1): the required period condition for the standard rate of the mobility component is met` d `with` `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` MEANS
        `regs 12(1)(a) and 13(1)(a): limb (a) is met` d `with` `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)`
    AND `regs 12 and 13: only limited ability is likely at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date` d

-- src:115 | (2) C meets the required period condition for the purposes of section 79(2) of the Act (mobility component at enhanced rate) where —
-- src:116 | (a) if C had been assessed at every time in the period of 3 months ending with the prescribed date, it is likely that the Secretary of State would have determined at that time that C had severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities; and
-- src:117 | (b) if C were to be assessed at every time in the period of 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date, it is likely that the Secretary of State would determine at that time that C had severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities.
@ref reg 13(2) (src:115-117)
GIVEN d IS A `the likely determinations across the two windows`
      `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 13(2): the required period condition for the enhanced rate of the mobility component is met` d `with` `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` MEANS
        `regs 12(2)(a) and 13(2)(a): limb (a) is met` d `with` `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)`
    AND d's `severely limited ability is likely to be determined at every time in the 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date`

-- The rate of a component for which the required period condition is met, from the text's own parentheticals:
-- 12(1)/13(1) are the standard rate (ss 78(1), 79(1)) and 12(2)/13(2) the enhanced rate (ss 78(2), 79(2)).
-- Where both are met (which reg 4(3) makes impossible on consistent facts) the enhanced rate is the higher.
GIVEN `the standard rate condition is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enhanced rate condition is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `a rate of a component`
`regs 12 and 13: the rate of the component whose required period condition is met` `the standard rate condition is met` `and` `the enhanced rate condition is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the enhanced rate condition is met` THEN `the enhanced rate of the component`
        IF `the standard rate condition is met` THEN `the standard rate of the component`
        OTHERWISE `no rate of the component`

§ `Regulation 14: the prescribed date`

-- reg 14(a): where C has made a claim for personal independence payment which has not been determined,
-- the prescribed date is the date of that claim or, if later, the earliest date in relation to which, if C
-- had been assessed at every time in the previous 3 months, it is likely that the Secretary of State would
-- have determined at that time that C had limited ability or, as the case may be, severely limited ability.
-- Where no such date exists the prescribed date is the date of the claim (fork F-13).
-- src:119 | Except where paragraph (2) or (3) of regulation 15 {repealed: or paragraph (2) or (3) of regulation 15A} , paragraph (2) or (3) of regulation 15A or paragraph (2) or (3) of regulation 15B applies, the prescribed date is–
-- src:120 | (a) where C has made a claim for personal independence payment which has not been determined, the date of that claim or, if later, the earliest date in relation to which, if C had been assessed in relation to C's ability to carry out daily living activities or, as the case may be, mobility activities, at every time in the previous 3 months, it is likely that the Secretary of State would have determined at that time that C had limited ability or, as the case may be, severely limited ability to carry out those activities; and
@ref reg 14(a) (src:119-120)
GIVEN `the date of the claim` IS A DATE
      `the earliest date from which limited or severely limited ability is likely to have been determined at every time in the previous 3 months` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 14(a): the prescribed date for a claim that has not been determined` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earliest date from which limited or severely limited ability is likely to have been determined at every time in the previous 3 months`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date of the claim`
    WHEN JUST e THEN
        IF e AT LEAST `the date of the claim` THEN e ELSE `the date of the claim`

-- reg 14(b): where C has an award of either or both components, each day of that award.
-- src:121 | (b) where C has an award of either or both components, each day of that award.
@ref reg 14(b) (src:121)
GIVEN `the day of the award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 14(b): the prescribed date on a day of an award` MEANS
    `the day of the award`

§ `Regulations 15, 15A and 15B: claims after an interval`

-- The dates the two windows hang from: the 3 months look back from the first, the 9 months look
-- forward from the day after the second.
DECLARE `the dates the required period condition is tested at` HAS
    `the date the 3 months look back from` IS A DATE
    `the date the 9 months look forward from` IS A DATE

-- reg 15(1)(b): the previous award ended not more than 2 years before the date on which the new claim is made.
-- Regulation 26(2)(b) reads "2 years" here as "1 year" for a claimant who has reached the relevant age; the
-- number of years enters reg 15(1) as an input, and this is the number the text prints.
-- src:125 | (b) C had a previous award for personal independence payment or adult disability payment which ended not more than 2 years before the date on which the new claim is made;
@ref reg 15(1)(b) (src:125)
`reg 15(1)(b): the number of years` MEANS 2

-- reg 15(1): paragraphs (2) and (3) apply where (a) C makes a claim (the new claim); (b) C had a previous
-- award of personal independence payment or adult disability payment which ended not more than 2 years before
-- the date on which the new claim is made; (c) the previous award consisted of the same component as the one
-- to which C is entitled (or would be entitled if C met the required period condition) under the new claim;
-- and (d) the Secretary of State determines that the entitlement under the new claim results from (i)
-- substantially the same physical or mental condition or conditions for which the previous award was made; or
-- (ii) a new condition which developed as a result of a condition for which the previous award was made.
-- The number of years in (b) is an input: `reg 15(1)(b): the number of years` is 2 as printed, and 1 where reg 26(2)(b) reads it so (reg 15(4)).
-- A previous award that ended on the day of the new claim, or before, is "not more than" the years before it.
-- src:123 | (1) Paragraphs (2) and (3) apply where—
-- src:124 | (a) C makes a claim for personal independence payment (“the new claim”);
-- src:125 | (b) C had a previous award for personal independence payment or adult disability payment which ended not more than 2 years before the date on which the new claim is made;
-- src:126 | (c) the previous award referred to in sub-paragraph (b), where that award was in respect of personal independence payment or adult disability payment, consisted of the same component as the one to which C is entitled (or would be entitled if C met the required period condition) under the new claim; and
-- src:127 | (d) the Secretary of State determines that the entitlement under the new claim results from-
-- src:128 | (i) substantially the same physical or mental condition or conditions for which the previous award was made; or
-- src:129 | (ii) a new physical or mental condition which developed as a result of a condition for which the previous award was made.
@ref reg 15(1) (src:123-129)
GIVEN `the benefit paid under the previous award` IS A `the benefit paid under an earlier award`
      `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day the new claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the number of years in regulation 15(1)(b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the previous award consisted of the same component as the new claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State determines that the entitlement results from substantially the same condition or conditions, or from a new condition that developed as a result of one of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 15(1): regulation 15(2) and (3) apply to the new claim` MEANS
        (   `the benefit paid under the previous award` EQUALS `personal independence payment`
         OR `the benefit paid under the previous award` EQUALS `adult disability payment`)
    AND `the day the previous award ended` AT MOST `the day the new claim is made`
    AND (`add years` `the day the previous award ended` `the number of years in regulation 15(1)(b)`) AT LEAST `the day the new claim is made`
    AND `the previous award consisted of the same component as the new claim`
    AND `the Secretary of State determines that the entitlement results from substantially the same condition or conditions, or from a new condition that developed as a result of one of them`

-- reg 15(2): in relation to determination of entitlement under the new claim (a) the prescribed date for regs
-- 12(1)(a) and (2)(a) and 13(1)(a) and (2)(a) is the date the previous award ended; and (b) regs 12(1)(b), (2)(b),
-- 13(1)(b) and (2)(b) have effect as if for "the prescribed date" were substituted "the date on which the new
-- claim for personal independence payment is made".
-- src:130 | (2) In relation to determination of entitlement under the new claim—
-- src:131 | (a) the prescribed date for the purposes of regulations 12(1)(a) and (2)(a) and 13(1)(a) and (2)(a) is the date on which the previous award ended where that award was in respect of personal independence payment or adult disability payment; and
-- src:132 | (b) regulations 12(1)(b) and (2)(b) and 13(1)(b) and (2)(b) have effect in relation to the new claim as if, for the words ‘the prescribed date’ there were substituted ‘the date on which the new claim for personal independence payment is made’.
@ref reg 15(2) (src:130-132)
GIVEN `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day the new claim is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
`reg 15(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` MEANS
    `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
        WITH `the date the 3 months look back from` IS `the day the previous award ended`
           , `the date the 9 months look forward from` IS `the day the new claim is made`

-- reg 15(3): where C is awarded either or both components under the new claim, in relation to continued
-- entitlement for the period of 3 months following the date of the new claim (a) as in (2)(a); and (b) regs
-- 12(1)(b) etc. have effect as if for "the prescribed date" were substituted "each day of the award".
-- src:133 | (3) Where C is awarded either or both components under the new claim, in relation to continued entitlement to that component or, as the case may be, those components, for the period of 3 months following the date of the new claim—
-- src:134 | (a) the prescribed date for the purposes of regulations 12(1)(a) and (2)(a) and 13(1)(a) and (2)(a) is the date on which the previous award ended where that award was in respect of personal independence payment or adult disability payment; and
-- src:135 | (b) regulations 12(1)(b) and (2)(b) and 13(1)(b) and (2)(b) have effect in relation to that award as if, for the words ‘the prescribed date’ there were substituted ‘each day of the award’.
@ref reg 15(3) (src:133-135)
GIVEN `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day of the award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
`reg 15(3): the dates for continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` MEANS
    `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
        WITH `the date the 3 months look back from` IS `the day the previous award ended`
           , `the date the 9 months look forward from` IS `the day of the award`

-- reg 15(4): this regulation is subject to regulation 26 (the number of years above; see pip-part6-age).
-- src:136 | (4) This regulation is subject to regulation 26.
@ref reg 15(4) (src:136)
`reg 15(4): regulation 15 is subject to regulation 26` MEANS
    "(4) This regulation is subject to regulation 26."

-- reg 15A(1)(b): the previous award of child disability payment ended not more than 2 years before the new claim.
-- src:140 | (b) C had a previous award of child disability payment which ended not more than 2 years before the date on which the new claim is made; and
@ref reg 15A(1)(b) (src:140)
`reg 15A(1)(b): the number of years` MEANS 2

-- reg 15A(1): paragraphs (2) to (5) apply where (a) C makes a claim (the new claim); (b) C had a previous award
-- of child disability payment which ended not more than 2 years before the date of the new claim; and (c) C
-- is aged 16 years or over at the date of the new claim. (The converter shows "{repealed: and (4)}" in the
-- opening words; paragraphs (2), (3), (4) and (5) are live.)
-- src:137 | 15A The prescribed date: claims for personal independence payment after award of Child Disability Payment
-- src:138 | (1) Paragraphs (2), (3) {repealed: and (4)} , (4) and (5) apply where—
-- src:139 | (a) C makes a claim for personal independence payment (“the new claim”);
-- src:140 | (b) C had a previous award of child disability payment which ended not more than 2 years before the date on which the new claim is made; and
-- src:141 | (c) C is aged 16 years or over at the date of the new claim.
@ref reg 15A(1) (src:137-141)
GIVEN `the benefit paid under the previous award` IS A `the benefit paid under an earlier award`
      `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day the new claim is made` IS A DATE
      `C's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 15A(1): regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply to the new claim` MEANS
        `the benefit paid under the previous award` EQUALS `child disability payment`
    AND `the day the previous award ended` AT MOST `the day the new claim is made`
    AND (`add years` `the day the previous award ended` `reg 15A(1)(b): the number of years`) AT LEAST `the day the new claim is made`
    AND (`add years` `C's date of birth` 16) AT MOST `the day the new claim is made`

-- src:142 | (2) In relation to determination of entitlement under the new claim—
-- src:143 | (a) the prescribed date for the purposes of regulations 12(1)(a) and (2)(a) and 13(1)(a) and (2)(a) is the date on which the previous award ended where that award was in respect of child disability payment; and
-- src:144 | (b) regulations 12(1)(b) and (2)(b) and 13(1)(b) and (2)(b) have effect in relation to the new claim as if, for the words “the prescribed date” there were substituted “the date on which the new claim for personal independence payment is made”.
@ref reg 15A(2) (src:142-144)
GIVEN `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day the new claim is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
`reg 15A(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` MEANS
    `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
        WITH `the date the 3 months look back from` IS `the day the previous award ended`
           , `the date the 9 months look forward from` IS `the day the new claim is made`

-- src:145 | (3) Where C is awarded either or both components under the new claim, in relation to entitlement to that component or, as the case may be, those components, for the period of 3 months following the date of the new claim—
-- src:146 | (a) the prescribed date for the purposes of regulations 12(1)(a) and (2)(a) and 13(1)(a) and (2)(a) is the date on which the previous award ended where that award was in respect of child disability payment; and
-- src:147 | (b) regulations 12(1)(b) and (2)(b) and 13(1)(b) and (2)(b) have effect in relation to that award as if, for the words “the prescribed date” there were substituted “each day of the award”.
@ref reg 15A(3) (src:145-147)
GIVEN `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day of the award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
`reg 15A(3): the dates for entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` MEANS
    `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
        WITH `the date the 3 months look back from` IS `the day the previous award ended`
           , `the date the 9 months look forward from` IS `the day of the award`

-- reg 15A(4) (and 15B(4)): C is to be regarded as meeting such of the conditions in reg 12(1)(a) or (2)(a) and
-- reg 13(1)(a) or (2)(a) (as modified) as are relevant to C's new claim, regardless of whether they have been met.
-- This is the input `limb (a) is regarded as met under regulation 15A(4) or 15B(4)` of regs 12 and 13; this rule
-- says when it is TRUE: whenever reg 15A(1) applies.
-- src:148 | (4) C is to be regarded as meeting such of the conditions contained in the following provisions of these Regulations (as modified by paragraphs (2) and (3) above) as are relevant to C’s new claim, regardless of whether those conditions have been met—
-- src:149 | (a) in regulation 12 (required period condition: daily living component), paragraph (1)(a) or (2)(a);
-- src:150 | (b) in regulation 13 (required period condition: mobility component), paragraph (1)(a) or (2)(a).
@ref reg 15A(4) (src:148-150)
GIVEN `regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply to the new claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 15A(4): limb (a) of regulations 12 and 13 is regarded as met` MEANS
    `regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply to the new claim`

-- reg 15A(5): where C makes the new claim during the 13 week period provided for in reg 36 of the Disability
-- Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021, the previous award is treated as having
-- ended immediately before C made the new claim: read as the day before the day of the claim.
-- out of text: Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021 reg 36
-- src:151 | (5) Where C makes the new claim during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 36 of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021, for the purpose of this regulation the previous award of child disability payment is to be treated as having ended immediately before C made the new claim.
@ref reg 15A(5) (src:151)
GIVEN `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day the new claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the new claim is made during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 36` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 15A(5): the day the previous child disability payment award is treated as having ended` MEANS
    IF `the new claim is made during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 36`
    THEN `the day the new claim is made` MINUS 1
    ELSE `the day the previous award ended`

-- reg 15B(1)(b): the previous award of Scottish adult disability living allowance ended not more than 2 years before
-- the new claim. Regulation 26A(2)(b) reads "2 years" here as "1 year" for a claimant who has reached the relevant age.
-- src:155 | (b) C had a previous award of Scottish adult disability living allowance which ended not more than 2 years before the date on which the new claim is made,
@ref reg 15B(1)(b) (src:155)
`reg 15B(1)(b): the number of years` MEANS 2

-- reg 15B(1): paragraphs (2) to (6) apply where (a) C makes a claim (the new claim); (b) C had a previous award of
-- Scottish adult disability living allowance which ended not more than 2 years before the date of the new claim;
-- (c) C has not been entitled to personal independence payment on any day since the end of that award; and (d) C was
-- 64 years old or younger on 8th April 2013 (so C had not reached the 65th birthday by that date).
-- src:153 | (1) Paragraphs (2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) apply where—
-- src:154 | (a) C makes a claim for personal independence payment (“the new claim”),
-- src:155 | (b) C had a previous award of Scottish adult disability living allowance which ended not more than 2 years before the date on which the new claim is made,
-- src:156 | (c) C has not been entitled to personal independence payment on any day since the end of the award of Scottish adult disability living allowance referred to in sub-paragraph (b), and
-- src:157 | (d) C was 64 years old or younger on 8th April 2013.
@ref reg 15B(1) (src:153-157)
GIVEN `the benefit paid under the previous award` IS A `the benefit paid under an earlier award`
      `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day the new claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the number of years in regulation 15B(1)(b)` IS A NUMBER
      `C has been entitled to personal independence payment on a day since the previous award ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 15B(1): regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim` MEANS
        `the benefit paid under the previous award` EQUALS `Scottish adult disability living allowance`
    AND `the day the previous award ended` AT MOST `the day the new claim is made`
    AND (`add years` `the day the previous award ended` `the number of years in regulation 15B(1)(b)`) AT LEAST `the day the new claim is made`
    AND (NOT `C has been entitled to personal independence payment on a day since the previous award ended`)
    AND (`add years` `C's date of birth` 65) GREATER THAN `the day 8th April 2013`

-- The date named in reg 15B(1)(d).
@ref reg 15B(1)(d) (src:157)
`the day 8th April 2013` MEANS YearMonthDay 2013 4 8

-- src:158 | (2) In relation to determination of entitlement under the new claim—
-- src:159 | (a) the prescribed date for the purposes of regulations 12(1)(a) and (2)(a) and 13(1)(a) and (2)(a) is the date on which the previous award ended where that award was in respect of Scottish adult disability living allowance, and
-- src:160 | (b) regulations 12(1)(b) and (2)(b) and 13(1)(b) and (2)(b) have effect in relation to the new claim as if for the words “the prescribed date” there were substituted “the date on which the new claim for personal independence payment is made”.
@ref reg 15B(2) (src:158-160)
GIVEN `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day the new claim is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
`reg 15B(2): the dates for determining entitlement under the new claim` MEANS
    `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
        WITH `the date the 3 months look back from` IS `the day the previous award ended`
           , `the date the 9 months look forward from` IS `the day the new claim is made`

-- src:161 | (3) Where C is awarded either or both components under the new claim, in relation to continued entitlement to that component or, as the case may be, those components, for the period of 3 months following the date of the new claim—
-- src:162 | (a) the prescribed date for the purposes of regulations 12(1)(a) and (2)(a) and 13(1)(a) and (2)(a) is the date on which the previous award ended where that award was in respect of Scottish disability living allowance, and
-- src:163 | (b) regulations 12(1)(b) and (2)(b) and 13(1)(b) and (2)(b) have effect in relation to that award as if for the words “the prescribed date” there were substituted “each day of the award”.
@ref reg 15B(3) (src:161-163)
GIVEN `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day of the award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
`reg 15B(3): the dates for continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim` MEANS
    `the dates the required period condition is tested at`
        WITH `the date the 3 months look back from` IS `the day the previous award ended`
           , `the date the 9 months look forward from` IS `the day of the award`

-- src:164 | (4) C is to be regarded as meeting such of the conditions contained in the following provisions of these Regulations (as modified by paragraphs (2) and (3) above) as are relevant to C's new claim, regardless of whether those conditions have been met—
-- src:165 | (a) in regulation 12 (required period condition: daily living component), paragraph (1)(a) or (2)(a);
-- src:166 | (b) in regulation 13 (required period condition: mobility component), paragraph (1)(a) or (2)(a).
@ref reg 15B(4) (src:164-166)
GIVEN `regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 15B(4): limb (a) of regulations 12 and 13 is regarded as met` MEANS
    `regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply to the new claim`

-- reg 15B(5): this regulation is subject to regulation 26A (see pip-part6-age).
-- src:167 | (5) This regulation is subject to regulation 26A (claim for personal independence payment after an award of Scottish adult disability living allowance and after reaching the relevant age).
@ref reg 15B(5) (src:167)
`reg 15B(5): regulation 15B is subject to regulation 26A` MEANS
    "(5) This regulation is subject to regulation 26A (claim for personal independence payment after an award of Scottish adult disability living allowance and after reaching the relevant age)."

-- reg 15B(6): where C makes the new claim during the 13 week period provided for in reg 48 of the Disability Assistance
-- (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025, the previous award is treated as having ended
-- immediately before C made the new claim.
-- out of text: Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025 reg 48
-- src:168 | (6) Where C makes the new claim during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 48 of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025, for the purpose of this regulation the previous award of Scottish adult disability living allowance is to be treated as having ended immediately before C made the new claim.
@ref reg 15B(6) (src:168)
GIVEN `the day the previous award ended` IS A DATE
      `the day the new claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the new claim is made during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 48` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 15B(6): the day the previous Scottish adult disability living allowance award is treated as having ended` MEANS
    IF `the new claim is made during the 13 week period provided for in regulation 48`
    THEN `the day the new claim is made` MINUS 1
    ELSE `the day the previous award ended`

§ `Which provision fixes the prescribed date`

-- Regs 14, 15, 15A and 15B each fix the dates; reg 14 applies "except where" paragraph (2) or (3) of reg 15, 15A or
-- 15B applies (src:119). Paragraph (2) is for determining entitlement under the new claim; paragraph (3) is for the
-- first 3 months of the award that follows it. The text does not say which prevails if the new claim meets the
-- conditions of more than one of regs 15, 15A and 15B (C having had two kinds of previous award), so that case is
-- not covered (fork F-14).
DECLARE `the stage at which the prescribed date is wanted` IS ONE OF
    `determining entitlement under the new claim`
    `continued entitlement in the 3 months following the new claim`

DECLARE `the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` IS ONE OF
    `regulation 14, there being no claim after an interval`
    `regulation 15(2)`
    `regulation 15(3)`
    `regulation 15A(2)`
    `regulation 15A(3)`
    `regulation 15B(2)`
    `regulation 15B(3)`
    `more than one of regulations 15, 15A and 15B applies, and the text does not say which prevails`

-- src:119 | Except where paragraph (2) or (3) of regulation 15 {repealed: or paragraph (2) or (3) of regulation 15A} , paragraph (2) or (3) of regulation 15A or paragraph (2) or (3) of regulation 15B applies, the prescribed date is–
@ref reg 14, reg 15(1), reg 15A(1), reg 15B(1) (src:119)
GIVEN `regulation 15(2) and (3) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      stage IS A `the stage at which the prescribed date is wanted`
GIVETH A `the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at`
`regs 14 to 15B: the provision that fixes the dates the required period condition is tested at` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    (`regulation 15(2) and (3) apply` AND `regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply`)
           OR (`regulation 15(2) and (3) apply` AND `regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply`)
           OR (`regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply` AND `regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply`)
        THEN `more than one of regulations 15, 15A and 15B applies, and the text does not say which prevails`
        IF `regulation 15(2) and (3) apply` AND stage EQUALS `determining entitlement under the new claim` THEN `regulation 15(2)`
        IF `regulation 15(2) and (3) apply` THEN `regulation 15(3)`
        IF `regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply` AND stage EQUALS `determining entitlement under the new claim` THEN `regulation 15A(2)`
        IF `regulation 15A(2) to (5) apply` THEN `regulation 15A(3)`
        IF `regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply` AND stage EQUALS `determining entitlement under the new claim` THEN `regulation 15B(2)`
        IF `regulation 15B(2) to (6) apply` THEN `regulation 15B(3)`
        OTHERWISE `regulation 14, there being no claim after an interval`
